# Mock EDC Project – Treatment Safety Monitoring Study

## Project Goal
This is a practice project to understand Electronic Data Capture (EDC) workflows in Clinical Data Management (CDM). All study data used for practice are fictional.

## eCRFs Practised

### 1. Demographics
- Subject ID
- Date of Birth
- Sex
- Informed Consent Date

### 2. Vitals
- Visit Date
- Systolic Blood Pressure
- Diastolic Blood Pressure
- Pulse
- Temperature

### 3. Adverse Events (AE)
- AE Term
- Start Date
- End Date
- Severity
- Serious (Yes/No)
- Outcome

## Edit Checks Practised
- Required-field checks
- Systolic BP practice range: 60–250 mmHg
- AE start date should not be earlier than informed consent date
- Review missing or inconsistent data

## Mock Query Practice
- Missing pulse
- Out-of-range blood pressure
- Missing informed consent date
- Inconsistent AE dates
- Missing visit date

## Key Learnings
- eCRF data entry
- Data validation and edit checks
- Query identification and documentation
- Importance of source data verification

## Screenshots
Screenshots of the Demographics, Vitals, and Adverse Events forms will be added to document the practice workflow.

## Disclaimer
This is a learning project using fictional practice data. It does not represent a live clinical trial or professional experience with a production EDC system.



